OL,3,GNEWSABlind 101-year-old veteran joins
OL,4,ACenotaph parade
OL,5,
OL,6,FA blind 101-year-old World War Two
OL,7,Fveteran honoured the fallen at the
OL,8,FCenotaph for the first time on
OL,9,FRemembrance Sunday.
OL,11,FGwynneth Pedler, from Dulwich,
OL,12,Fsouth-east London, joined more than 40
OL,13,Fother blind veterans at the parade.
OL,15,FPedler joined the Women's Royal Naval
OL,16,FService (WRNS) in 1944 and was posted
OL,17,Fto Crail, near St Andrews, where she
OL,18,Fworked as an air mechanic. She cleaned
OL,19,Fand maintained the guns used by airmen
OL,20,Fwho were learning to drop torpedoes.
OL,23,APub: 08-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
